{%- comment -%}
  Announcement bar: one short line above the header, in the header group, so it is on every
  page. Its default is a fact the store can prove ("Envío gratis a todo el país"): no
  exclamation mark, no countdown, no link, no urgency. A blank line renders nothing, which
  is also how the owner turns it off.

  Seen without shouting: a filled brand band with on-brand text at body-lg. Contrast is
  on-brand on brand, 5.18 to 1 in the light theme and 8.21 to 1 in the dark one (4.5 needed).
  The bar and the header stay at the top of the screen on scroll, together: the CSS makes
  both header group wrappers sticky and sets the header's offset to the bar's fixed height.
  The text is one line; a longer one is cut with an ellipsis rather than growing the bar.

  NOT dismissible, on purpose. Closing it would need a script and somewhere to remember the
  choice (a cookie or localStorage), the bar would flash on every page until that ran, and
  the line is information the customer is glad to see again on the cart. The cost is 44px at
  the top of every screen, the bar being fixed in place; if the bar ever carries something
  temporary, revisit this.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
  {{ 'section-announcement-bar.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <div class="announcement-bar">
    <p class="announcement-bar__text text-body-lg container">{{ section.settings.text }}</p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.announcement-bar.name",
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "t:sections.announcement-bar.settings.text.label",
      "info": "t:sections.announcement-bar.settings.text.info",
      "default": "t:sections.announcement-bar.settings.text.default"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.announcement-bar.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
